    <h3>Job &amp; Mentorship Opportunities</h3>
    <p>These are positions and mentorship opportunities we're particularly excited about!</p>

    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <h4>Effective Thesis</h4>
        <p><a href="https://effectivethesis.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Effective Thesis</a> is a project that aims to help students find thesis topics with high potential to improve the world, regardless of their location and degree level. They offer <em>free</em> coaching to help students develop thesis topic ideas, connect students with expert researchers, suggest potential supervisors, and find relevant opportunities for students such as funding and internships. You can find all the research directions we recommend and apply for coaching on <a href="https://effectivethesis.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">their site</a>.</p>

        <h4>Open Philanthropy Biosecurity Scholarships</h4>
        <p>This program aims to provide flexible support for a small group of people early in their careers to pursue work and study related to <a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5576209/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">global catastrophic biological risks</a> (GCBRs), events in which biological agents could lead to sudden, extraordinary, and widespread disaster. Open Philanthropy's goal is to reduce <a href="https://www.openphilanthropy.org/focus/global-catastrophic-risks" target="_blank" rel="noopener">risks to humanity's long-run future</a>. <!-- TODO: confirm this scholarship and its current deadline are still active --> Check Open Philanthropy's site for current application deadlines.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>ALLFED Volunteer</h4>
        <p>The <a href="https://allfed.info/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Alliance to Feed the Earth in Disasters (ALLFED)</a> and <a href="https://www.foodsystemshandbook.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Food Systems Handbook (FSH)</a> are currently looking for students with a range of disciplinary backgrounds and interests. You can also reach out to Adin Richards (adin_richards@brown.edu) with any questions.</p>
        <p>Fill out this <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScG4xaIMjfjVr2_hQZAo-iWgd0FvEwQaQ_tGhj4y6lGzWmb6A/formResponse" target="_blank" rel="noopener">form</a> if you'd be interested in working with them!</p>
      </div>
